			<div class="content" id="post-content-1675104">
									

<p>I might not explaining it right in the article. The real-life Voyager 1 will pass (actually it will be about 1.6 light years away, but this is its closest approach to a star) Gliese 445 in 40,000 years or so, hence the date I choose.</p>
<p>From this point on the Foundation doesn't know what is true or not and so wouldn't mention it in the description, beyond the facts.</p>
<p>The culture-changing comes from the aliens listening to our radio transmissions. This can occur at any time in the next 40,000 years. Voyager is not involved at this point. The bombing would occur close to the date I said in-article.</p>
<p>While the aliens debated destroying us or not, Voyager arrived, and the aliens responded to us, now, using faster-than-light travel. The way something moves through time above the speed of light, is <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_travel#Via_faster-than-light_.28FTL.29_travel">theoretically</a> (obviously this has never been demonstrated to be true) backwards.</p>

